.IX Title "Clownfish::CharBuf 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::CharBuf 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::CharBuf \- Growable buffer holding Unicode characters.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 4
\&    my $buf = Clownfish::CharBuf\->new;
\&    $buf\->cat(\*(Aqabc\*(Aq);
\&    $buf\->cat_char(ord("\en"));
\&    print $buf\->to_string;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 3
\&    my $char_buf = Clownfish::CharBuf\->new(
\&        capacity => $capacity,  # default: 0
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Return a new CharBuf.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBcapacity\fR \- Initial minimum capacity of the CharBuf, in bytes.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS cat
.IX Subsection "cat"
.Vb 1
\&    $char_buf\->cat($string);
.Ve
.PP
Concatenate the contents of String \f(CW\*(C`string\*(C'\fR onto the end of the
caller.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBstring\fR \- The String to concatenate.
.SS cat_char
.IX Subsection "cat_char"
.Vb 1
\&    $char_buf\->cat_char($code_point);
.Ve
.PP
Concatenate one Unicode character onto the end of the CharBuf.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBcode_point\fR \- The code point of the Unicode character.
.SS grow
.IX Subsection "grow"
.Vb 1
\&    $char_buf\->grow($capacity);
.Ve
.PP
Assign more memory to the CharBuf, if it doesn’t already have enough
room to hold a string of \f(CW\*(C`size\*(C'\fR bytes.  Cannot shrink the
allocation.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBcapacity\fR \- The new minimum capacity of the ByteBuf.
.SS clear
.IX Subsection "clear"
.Vb 1
\&    $char_buf\->clear();
.Ve
.PP
Clear the CharBuf.
.SS get_size
.IX Subsection "get_size"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $char_buf\->get_size();
.Ve
.PP
Return the size of the CharBuf’s content in bytes.
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $char_buf\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Return a clone of the object.
.SS yield_string
.IX Subsection "yield_string"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $char_buf\->yield_string();
.Ve
.PP
Return the content of the CharBuf as String and clear the CharBuf.
This is more efficient than \fBto_string()\fR.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::CharBuf isa Clownfish::Obj.
